ttycity for Atari System V and AMIX
===================================

ttycity is tenox7's port of Micropolis (the open-source SimCity) to
curses terminals (github.com/tenox7/ttycity), built as a static AMIX
program.  On Atari System V it runs through the service pack's amx module
(github.com/slaapliedje/atari-sysv-sp1).

    ttycity                       monochrome
    TERM=xterm-color ttycity      8 colours, in an xterm or over telnet
                                  from a colour terminal

The system's "xterm" terminal entry has no colour, so the package brings
an "xterm-color" one (share/terminfo; its source is doc/xterm-color.ti)
and the ttycity command uses it when TERM is xterm-color.  The mouse and
the Unicode mode are not built: SVR4 curses has neither.

Installed under /opt/ttycity (bin, lib, share/cities, doc), with
/usr/bin/ttycity linking to the command.

Install as root:   pkgadd -d ttycity-VERSION.pkg TTYCITY
Remove:            pkgrm TTYCITY

Source: github.com/slaapliedje/asv-games has the build scripts, the one
source change and the exact upstream commit.  Licence: GPL-3.0 with the
Micropolis additional terms (LICENSE here).
